<div class="wrap">
<header>
<h1>The List</h1>
<div class="sub">Fifteen domaines in Burgundy and the Northern Rhône — and the aesthetic extracted from them.</div>
<div class="meta"><span>reconstructed <b>2026-10-06</b></span>
<span>sources <b>two conversations · 2025-04-25 → 2026-02-12</b></span>
<span><b>15</b> domaines · <b>2</b> registers · <b>1</b> control problem</span></div>
</header>

<div class="orig">
<p><span class="q">“We met the folks from these domaines…”</span> — an encounter list, kept as given, with the ask it carried: <em>the most terse but insightful brief on each one; the pattern that binds all of them; something irreplaceable, to be abstracted and composed into an aesthetic — expressed first in images and seals.</em></p>
<p class="small">The rule set with it, day one: the list is strong evidence of contact with a serious wine milieu; it is weaker evidence of one individual’s aesthetic preferences. This page is the reconstruction: the list, fifteen briefs, the pattern, the manifesto.</p>
</div>

<h2>1 · The list, as given</h2>
<dl class="list">
<dt>Burgundy</dt><dd>Fourrier · Bruno Clair · De guellec · Marechal · Drouhin · Simon Bize · Lafarge · Duroche · Jacques Carillon</dd>
<dt>Rhône</dt><dd>Clape · Eric Texier · Emmanuel Darnaud · Rousset · Levet · Gonon</dd>
</dl>
<p class="small" style="margin-top:10px">Spelling preserved. Names are not silently completed — where an identity stayed open, it stays open below.</p>

<h2>2 · Fifteen briefs</h2>
<div class="legend"><span><b>●</b> explicit</span><span><b>◐</b> probable</span><span><b>○</b> unresolved</span>
<span class="small">provenance scale: explicit → probable → inferred → unresolved</span></div>
<div class="rows">
<div class="row"><span class="n">01</span><span class="who"><b>Fourrier</b><span>Gevrey-Chambertin</span></span><span class="what"><p>Old vines, minimal handling, little new oak; a silken Pinot that whispers its site.</p><span class="lesson">→ Protect the signal from handling.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">02</span><span class="who"><b>Bruno Clair</b><span>Marsannay → eight villages</span></span><span class="what"><p>Classicist with a modern edge; whole-cluster and extraction decided per appellation, never one recipe.</p><span class="lesson">→ Structure makes nuance durable.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">03</span><span class="who"><b>Le Guellec-Ducouet</b><span>listed as “De guellec” · Gevrey / Brochon</span></span><span class="what"><p>Young domaine (2018) on family vineyards whose history goes back to 1920; limited-production Pinot, powerful yet delicate.</p><span class="lesson">→ Identity: probable (medium confidence) — kept open, not completed.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="prob">◐</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">04</span><span class="who"><b>Maréchal</b><span>Burgundy · ~8 ha</span></span><span class="what"><p>Elegant, meticulous, small-scale. <b>Identity unresolved</b> — several Burgundy Maréchals exist; deliberately not guessed.</p><span class="lesson">→ Directness need not become crudity.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="unr">○</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">05</span><span class="who"><b>Joseph Drouhin</b><span>Burgundy, since 1880</span></span><span class="what"><p>An institution (~100 ha) that treats vineyard diversity as its organizing principle rather than collapsing it into one prestige style.</p><span class="lesson">→ A broad grammar can preserve continuity.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">06</span><span class="who"><b>Simon Bize</b><span>Savigny-lès-Beaune</span></span><span class="what"><p>Organic and biodynamic work; purity, structure, longevity — a quiet form containing firm structure.</p><span class="lesson">→ Quiet form may contain firm structure.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">07</span><span class="who"><b>Lafarge</b><span>Volnay</span></span><span class="what"><p>Family continuity reaching into the early 1800s; a biodynamic pioneer whose patience converts continuity into depth.</p><span class="lesson">→ Patience converts continuity into depth.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">08</span><span class="who"><b>Duroché</b><span>Gevrey-Chambertin</span></span><span class="what"><p>Fifth generation; elegant, transparent; breaks one village into many named sites and keeps them distinct.</p><span class="lesson">→ Precision can remain muscular.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">09</span><span class="who"><b>Jacques Carillon</b><span>Puligny-Montrachet</span></span><span class="what"><p>An old Puligny family; mineral-driven whites, restrained oak, clarity through proportion.</p><span class="lesson">→ Clarity depends upon proportion.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">10</span><span class="who"><b>Clape</b><span>Cornas</span></span><span class="what"><p>Deep continuity; steep terraces, whole clusters, concrete and old foudres — force organized, not removed.</p><span class="lesson">→ Time integrates severity.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">11</span><span class="who"><b>Éric Texier</b><span>Brézème and neglected places</span></span><span class="what"><p>Returned attention to places whose former significance had largely disappeared — recovery, not rebellion.</p><span class="lesson">→ Recover what dominant maps omitted.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">12</span><span class="who"><b>Emmanuel Darnaud</b><span>Crozes-Hermitage</span></span><span class="what"><p>Estate dates to 2001; parcels vinified separately so their differences survive — modest scale intensifying decision.</p><span class="lesson">→ Modest scale can intensify decision.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">13</span><span class="who"><b>Rousset</b><span>probably Stéphane Rousset · Crozes / Saint-Joseph</span></span><span class="what"><p>Parcels span granite, loess and alluvial contexts; geology defeats generic regional identity. <span class="small">(high confidence)</span></p><span class="lesson">→ Geology defeats generic identity.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="prob">◐</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">14</span><span class="who"><b>Levet</b><span>Côte-Rôtie · Ampuis</span></span><span class="what"><p>A small family lineage in a traditional register; wild and structured, needing age to reveal itself.</p><span class="lesson">→ Irregularity can carry identity.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
<div class="row"><span class="n">15</span><span class="who"><b>Gonon</b><span>Saint-Joseph</span></span><span class="what"><p>Rooted in the historic core; whole-cluster, vivid, lifted — wildness that becomes clear when held.</p><span class="lesson">→ Wildness becomes clear when held.</span></span><span class="mk"><i class="exp">●</i></span></div>
</div>
<p class="small" style="margin-top:10px">These are working hypotheses, not rankings. The pattern, if any, lives one level above style.</p>

<h2>3 · The pattern</h2>
<p class="small">The first synthesis — “elegance, purity, terroir, minimal intervention” — was rejected: it erased real differences among the makers. What survived, and the strongest line the thread would defend:</p>
<p style="font:700 19px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:14px 0">Place becomes perceptible when intervention is disciplined but not erased.</p>
<p>The control problem, not an amount: <b>“Do enough to make difference legible; not so much that the intervention becomes the subject.”</b> The thread named the result <b class="news">high-fidelity particularism</b> — this hillside, this year, this inherited material; enough craft that the differences survive transmission.</p>

<h3>The operators — an operator set, never a classification of makers</h3>
<div class="loop">
<div><div class="m">TRACE</div><div class="o">Reveal distinctions already present</div><div class="s">inner state: attention</div><div class="f">fails as: preciousness</div></div>
<div><div class="m">BEAR</div><div class="o">Give pressure a form that can endure</div><div class="s">inner state: composure</div><div class="f">fails as: rigidity</div></div>
<div><div class="m">RELEASE</div><div class="o">Permit life, variance and surprise</div><div class="s">inner state: responsiveness</div><div class="f">fails as: shapelessness</div></div>
<div><div class="m">RETURN</div><div class="o">Compare outcome with origin</div><div class="s">what did transformation reveal —</div><div class="f">and what did it erase?</div></div>
</div>
<div class="loopnote">TRACE → BEAR → RELEASE → RETURN ↺ &nbsp;·&nbsp; recursive, not categorical. &nbsp;·&nbsp; questions: <em>What changes when almost nothing changes? What form can carry this pressure without concealing it? Which inherited constraint is essential, and which merely became habitual?</em></div>

<h3>Four attitudes inside the list (a reading that survived verification)</h3>
<div class="fam">
<div><div class="fn">CARTOGRAPHERS</div><div class="fc">subdivide until a meaningful difference appears</div><div class="fm">Fourrier · Bruno Clair · Duroché · Carillon</div></div>
<div><div class="fn">CUSTODIANS</div><div class="fc">tradition = longitudinal dataset</div><div class="fm">Lafarge · Simon Bize · Clape · Gonon · Levet</div></div>
<div><div class="fn">ARCHAEOLOGISTS</div><div class="fc">novelty can consist of recovering a resolution the present has forgotten</div><div class="fm">Texier · Le Guellec-Ducouet</div></div>
<div><div class="fn">INTEGRATORS</div><div class="fc">how large can a system become without collapsing local distinction?</div><div class="fm">Drouhin · Maréchal · Darnaud · Rousset</div></div>
</div>

<h3>Seven laws — held falsifiable</h3>
<ol class="laws">
<li>Use few primitives.</li>
<li>Make small differences consequential.</li>
<li>Preserve provenance through transformation.</li>
<li>Adapt treatment to material; never impose one effect everywhere.</li>
<li>Hide labour, not structure.</li>
<li>Permit delayed disclosure.</li>
<li>Compress the whole while differentiating the interior.</li>
</ol>
<p class="small" style="margin-top:8px">If several makers break a law, the law dies. These are the lines that survived; everything downstream — colour, texture, glyph, scale, fragrance — is downstream.</p>

<div class="quotes">
<p><b>“Maximum identity from minimum vocabulary.”</b></p>
<p>“Do not make variants different by changing their vocabulary. Make variants different by allowing the same vocabulary to encounter different conditions.”</p>
<p>“Importance does not require visual magnitude.” — a 2 mm interruption can matter more than an added dragon; <b>high semantic consequence per unit difference</b>.</p>
<p>“Differentiate internally; compress externally.” — Burgundy teaches differentiation, the Rhône compression. Tendencies, not personalities.</p>
<p>“Do not maximize detail. Maximize <b>consequential detail</b>.”</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:0">“Global coherence + locally inexhaustible differentiation.”</p>
</div>

<h2>4 · The manifesto — the art of cultivated difference</h2>
<div class="manifesto">
<div class="mt">THE ART OF CULTIVATED DIFFERENCE</div>
<p>Attend before naming. The world does not lack form. It is obscured by handling.</p>
<p>Reveal the difference that changes the whole. Give that difference a body. Let the body endure without becoming a prison.</p>
<p>Do not confuse silence with emptiness. Do not confuse force with volume. Do not confuse irregularity with freedom. Do not confuse inheritance with truth.</p>
<p>Line must disclose. Mass must carry. Variation must remain answerable to identity.</p>
<p>Preserve grain. Expose joints. Remove interference before adding expression. Intensify only what can survive intensification.</p>
<p>A tradition lives when its function crosses into a new carrier. A structure lives when it permits transformation without losing memory. An artifact succeeds when it alters perception, survives use and generates further use.</p>
<p>Trace what is present. Bear what is real. Release what can become.</p>
<p>Make nothing merely impressive. Make the invisible difference operative.</p>
<div class="tiny">distilled line: “Reveal the difference; build it a body; leave it capable of becoming.”</div>
</div>

<h2>5 · Limits</h2>
<div class="limits">
<p><b>Not a canon.</b> The list records encounters — “we met the folks” — not favourites. It is strong evidence of a milieu, weaker evidence of one person’s taste.</p>
<p><b>Not “minimal intervention.”</b> The makers differ materially in farming, stems, extraction, scale and oak. The operable phrase is <b>intervention subordinated to identity</b> — the maker present, technique not becoming the subject.</p>
<p><b>No painter, perfume or genre per producer.</b> Regions are tendencies, not personalities; the interesting object is the relationship between maker and difference.</p>
<p><b>Unresolved stays unresolved.</b> One wrongly completed name would contaminate the pattern (see 04, 03, 13).</p>
<p class="small">Sources: two conversations — <em>Wine Domaines Deep Dive</em> (2025-04-25) and <em>Aesthetic Exploration of Wine</em> (2026-02-12). Reconstructed 2026-10-06 from the transcripts; quotes verbatim; corrections welcome. Noindex reading surface.</p>
</div>

<footer>
<div class="fin">“To be expressed in the design and painting of images and seals; music is fine; and thirdly, in priority, scent or flavour.” — the brief</div>
the list · reconstruction 2026-10-06 · one page, fifteen domaines, one discipline
</footer>
</div>